Introducing Spartan, a novel approach for training neural networks with pre-defined sparsity. This method effectively leverages a combination of two techniques: soft parameter pruning through optimal transportation and hard parameter sparsification during forward passes. This dynamic balance enables initial exploration of various sparsity patterns and gradually shifts towards maximizing accuracy with a predetermined level of sparsity. Spartan offers the flexibility to be applied to any neural network and can be paired with both traditional sparsification methods or advanced pattern-based sparsification techniques. When integrated with a cutting-edge efficient sparsification method, it can achieve impressive sparsity levels (e.g. 90%) in image classification tasks on the ResNet50 architecture on the ImageNet dataset, yielding performance comparable to the dense model, while also reducing computational requirements significantly. The source code for Spartan is publicly available. 

